  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Preheat oven to 240°C/220°C fan-forced.\n• In a medium bowl, place haloumi and cover with water to soak.\n• Cut potato into fries and place on the lined oven tray. Sprinkle with BBQ spice blend, season with salt and drizzle with olive oil.\n• Toss to coat and bake until tender, 20-25 mins.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-671a4137c2f9d9459122c739-61d0425b.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, thinly slice cucumber into half-moons. Grate carrot. Finely chop or crush garlic.\n• In a small bowl, combine the honey, white wine vinegar, garlic, a pinch of chilli flakes (if using) and a splash of water.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-671a4137c2f9d9459122c739-caba666e.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• When fries have 10 mins remaining, drain haloumi and pat dry. Cut the haloumi into 1cm-thick slices.\n• In a medium frying pan, heat a drizzle of olive oil over medium-high heat.\n• Cook haloumi until golden brown, 1-2 mins each side. Cook haloumi in batches if necessary.\n• Remove pan from heat and add hot honey mixture, turning haloumi to coat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-671a4137c2f9d9459122c739-75610124.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• In a second medium bowl, combine cucumber, carrot, salad leaves and a drizzle of white wine vinegar and olive oil. Season.\n• Divide hot honey-glazed haloumi, seasoned fries and cucumber salad between plates.\n• Drizzle any remaining glaze from the pan over haloumi. Serve with the mayonnaise.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-671a4137c2f9d9459122c739-9fcf8173.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
